# Controls what `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads to Cloud Build.
#
# The corpus lives in Qdrant now, so the image needs NO data at all — see the
# Dockerfile header and .dockerignore, which excludes data/ outright. Every
# byte of data/ we upload here is therefore paid for twice (Cloud Build ingress
# + a source archive kept in GCS forever) and then discarded by the build.
#
# This file used to preserve data/chroma for the old Chroma-in-the-image
# architecture, which meant ~2.4 GB per deploy of pure waste. Keep data/
# excluded wholesale; if the image ever needs a data file again, add that ONE
# path back rather than reopening the directory.

.git/
.github/
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
results/
notebooks/
tests/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# The whole corpus — 6.5 GB locally, none of it wanted by the build.
data/
chroma.tar.gz
